      "math_academy_id": "q-161572",
      "sequence_position": 10,
      "problem": "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{1-y-z}24y\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{1}{2},\\,0\\le z\\le y\\}.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{1-y-z}24y\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}24y[x]_{x=0}^{x=1-y-z}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}24y(1-y-z)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}24y-24{y}^{2}-24yz\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}24y-24{y}^{2}-24yz\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}{\\int }_{0}^{y}24(y-{y}^{2})-24yz\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}24(y-{y}^{2})[z]_{z=0}^{z=y}-12y[{z}^{2}]_{z=0}^{z=y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}24(y-{y}^{2})y-12{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}24{y}^{2}-36{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[8{y}^{3}-9{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=1/2} \\\\  & =8(\\frac{1}{8}-0)-9(\\frac{1}{16}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
